        "review": {
          "evidence": {
            "engineering-quality": {
              "availability": "available",
              "findings": [
                {
                  "evidence": "template/scripts/execute_requirement.py, in the `if not ordered:` branch of the sequential block, `_await_post_merge(..., rebind=rebound)` carries it. The `_retrospective_pending(...)` and `reconcile_parent(...)` returns on the lines after it do not. A rebind that happens on the pass that finishes the chain is therefore not reported to the operator on those paths. The receipt file is still written.",
                  "id": "rebind-receipt-dropped-on-terminal-paths",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "The rebind audit record is surfaced in only some return paths of advance."
                },
                {
                  "evidence": "In `_rebind_sequential`, `json.loads(manifest.read_text(...)).get(\"change\")` is not wrapped in try/except. A malformed or unreadable manifest raises JSONDecodeError or OSError instead of RequirementExecutionError. A manifest whose JSON is not an object also raises AttributeError. The other new readers (`_sequential_order`, `rank`) convert these errors explicitly. `orchestrate_pre_authoring._affected_sources` does use the guarded `_load_json`.",
                  "id": "rebind-unguarded-manifest-read",
                  "severity": "advisory",
                  "summary": "`_rebind_sequential` reads bundle manifests without error handling, so a bad manifest raises a raw exception."
                }
              ],
              "perspective": "engineering-quality",
